# Physiological Developmental Stages Across the Human Lifespan
#
# Perinatal neurodevelopment, childhood immune priming, pubertal remodeling, and prefrontal consolidation.

#>spw_cache_physio_stages
#:cache #!physio_dev
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Model the biochemical, endocrine, and morphological transformations characterizing human developmental critical windows."
  ~#biological_axes: "Neurogenesis, myelination, epiphyseal osteogenesis, endocrine axis maturation, and cellular senescence"
}

^["perinatal_and_first_thousand_days"]{
  critical_window: "Conception through age two: The most rapid phase of brain growth and epigenetic calibration in the human lifespan."
  biological_milestones: #[
    "Cortical DHA Incorporation: High-affinity uptake of docosahexaenoic acid into neuronal cell membranes governing synaptogenesis",
    "Microbiome Seeding: Pioneer colonization by Bifidobacterium infantis digesting human milk oligosaccharides (HMOs) to seal gut enterocytes",
    "Iron-Dependent Oligodendrocyte Maturation: Essential ferritin concentrations required for rapid myelin sheath synthesis in white matter tracts",
    "Choline & Folate Methylation: One-carbon metabolism driving widespread histone and DNA methylation for cellular differentiation"
  ]
}

^["childhood_somatic_growth_and_immune_priming"]{
  developmental_focus: "Ages two through ten: Thymic immune education, motor coordination refinement, and structural bone growth."
  mechanisms: .{
    thymic_education: "Negative selection eliminating autoreactive T-cells while training adaptive recognition against environmental pathogens"
    growth_plate_osteogenesis: "Chondrocyte proliferation stimulated by pulsatile Growth Hormone (GH) and hepatic Insulin-like Growth Factor 1 (IGF-1)"
    synaptic_pruning: "Microglia engulfing low-activity dendritic spines to increase neural transmission efficiency and sensory processing"
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["pubertal_endocrine_and_skeletal_remodeling"]{
  neuroendocrine_switch: "Disinhibition of hypothalamic Kisspeptin neurons triggering pulsatile gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH) release."
  morphological_transformations: #[
    "Peak Bone Mass Accretion: Accumulation of up to 50% of adult lifetime bone mineral density within a 3-4 year window",
    "Sex-Steroid Remodeling: Estradiol driving pelvic widening and trabecular density; Testosterone stimulating myofibrillar hypertrophy and erythropoiesis",
    "Epiphyseal Plate Mineralization: Estrogen-dependent closure of chondrocytic growth zones concluding linear height potential",
    "Circadian Phase Delay: A biological shift of 2+ hours in pineal melatonin release onset, naturally pushing adolescent chronotype later"
  ]
}

^["young_adult_prefrontal_consolidation"]{
  age_range: "Ages eighteen through twenty-six: Final structural stabilization of executive cognitive architecture."
  hallmarks: #[
    "Prefrontal Cortex Myelination: Insulating frontolimbic inhibitory circuits, enabling impulse control, future planning, and risk calculation",
    "Peak Functional Capacity: Optimal muscular cross-sectional area, mitochondrial density, and maximal oxygen uptake (VO2 max)",
    "Metabolic Flexibility: High glycogen storage capacity and rapid lipid oxidation under physical exertion"
  ]
}

^["midlife_and_senescent_homeostasis"]{
  gerotargets: "Ages forty and beyond: Shifting biological resources toward genomic maintenance, proteostasis, and mitochondrial repair."
  pathways: #[
    "Endocrine Transitions: Perimenopausal ovarian follicle depletion (precipitous estrogen drop) and gradual male andropause (1% annual testosterone decline)",
    "Sarcopenia & Osteopenia Defense: Countering accelerated muscle loss and trabecular thinning through mechanical resistance and dietary leucine",
    "Senescent Cell Clearance: Autophagy-driven degradation of damaged organelle populations and clearing of pro-inflammatory SASP secretomes"
  ]
}

^["taste"]{
  ~#taste: "Development is not a monotonic accumulation of years, but a sequence of unrepeatable alchemical transformations."
  ~#wonder: "Why does the human adolescent brain remain deliberately unmyelinated in its frontal lobes for nearly a decade, risking impulsivity in exchange for creative adaptability?"

  principles: #[
    "Critical windows are non-fungible: A missed micronutrient during embryonic neurulation cannot be fully compensated by supplements in adulthood.",
    "Biphasic adaptation: Stress and challenge (hormesis) within physiological tolerance strengthen tissue; chronic unabated distress degrades it.",
    "Chronobiological respect: Honoring the natural shifts in sleep, appetite, and energy that accompany each epoch of human maturation."
  ]
}

^"invariants"{
  "Adolescent bone mineral accrual requires adequate co-presence of Calcium, Vitamin D3, Vitamin K2, and mechanical impact loading.",
  "Thyroid hormone (T3/T4) and Iron levels must remain optimal throughout embryonic and early childhood neurogenesis to prevent cognitive deficit.",
  "Epiphyseal plate fusion permanently terminates longitudinal skeletal growth, demarcating the end of somatic height accretion.",
}

#>wonder_physio_stages_1
?["How does the timing of adolescent pubertal onset impact lifelong longevity and bone mineral density?"]{
  #:depth #!biological ~#lens(endocrine_chronobiology)
  ~#hypothesis: "Pulsatile gonadotropin onset delayed by 18 months via nutrient-dense, low-endocrine-disruptor diets correlates with a 15% increase in peak adult bone density and reduced adult hormone-dependent cancer risks."
  !probe{ "Conduct 30-year epidemiological cohort analysis tracking Tanner stage progression against adult DXA scans and metabolic markers." }
  $%[endocrine.pubertal_timing_months, osteogenesis.adult_femoral_bmd]
}
